<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theobald I of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1201–1253</span> · Also known as Theobald IV of Champagne, Theobald the Troubadour</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theobald I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1234 and, as Theobald IV, count of Champagne from his birth in 1201. One of the most admired trouvères, or poets, of his age, he wrote love songs and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> songs, and he led the Barons' Crusade of 1239–1240 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>. His accession brought Navarre under a French dynasty, the House of Champagne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theobald-i-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Theobald I of Navarre" width="160" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymus (Chansons de Thibaut I de Navarre) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theobald_I_of_Navarre_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
